{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And HaShem said to Moses, 'Here I am' etc.</b> The verse does not say ״לֵאמֹר״ ('to say'). Also, it began speaking in the second person and concluded in the third person: ״וְיָצָא הָעָם״ ('and the people shall go out') etc. This may be explained according to the statement of the Sages, of blessed memory (Yoma 75a), that the manna descended for the righteous at the entrance of each one's tent and he had no need to go out after it, whereas for the rest of the people it descended in another place and they would go out to gather it. And this is what it says: <b>Here I am raining down bread for you</b> etc. — meaning, without any need to go out to gather; but the people shall go out and gather. In correspondance to their lack of faith and having asked prematurely, they will obtain it with exertion." "<b>And the reason</b> it did not say at the beginning of this prophecy ״לֵאמֹר״ ('to say'), is because He would yet command him a second time all the matters in the passage that follows this one; rather, He preempted the matters to Moses so that he might find the response in his mouth, and immediately and at once He answered them, for the prophecy was spoken to him in the blink of an eye, and immediately and at once: ״וְהִנֵּה כְבוֹד ה׳״ ('and behold, the glory of HaShem')." "<b>That I may test them etc.</b> For bread from heaven requires no preparation at all, and through this they would be free from everything, and I will see whether they will walk etc." "<b>Further,</b> it intends on this basis the reason of <b>a day's portion in its day, that I may test them</b> — when he will need every day for his sustenance:"], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:28:39.140113056Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}